 this right now.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5816416765/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":2,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5950559593","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116415#issuecomment-5950559593","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116415","id":5950559593,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABYq5VaQ","user":{"login":"Arnklit","id":4955051,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5NTUwNTE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4955051?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit","html_url":"https://github.com/Arnklit","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-02T10:38:41Z","updated_at":"2026-10-02T10:43:27Z","body":"I can't see my way out of adding physics interpolation into this without doing a separate PR that adds that functionality for 2d to the engine.\r\n\r\nI'm investigating doing that work. It seems that the 2D interpolation works on local transforms, rather than global like the 3D ones, so it's not a straight copy of the 3D system to set up the code that tracks and interpolates when calling `get_global_transform_interpolated()`\r\n\r\n@QbieShay do you think it makes sense to merge as is, without physics interpolation. I added a note about it to the documentation and the node is marked experimental like the 3d one. \r\n\r\nAlso I copied the implementation for shortening the trail from your trail3d work. I see that you attributed CozyCubeGames in your implementation, should I do that here as well?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5950559593/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]